                <pb facs="0482" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            Durham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Foster, in reply to Mr. Durham’s telegram, informs him that the Department
                    will consider what is the proper course to adopt in the event of an
                    unconditional refusal of indemnity, but that while diplomatic negotiations are
                    pending the President is unwilling to have any naval demonstration.</p>
            </div>
